course: dictionary
lesson: 11572
title: Animate: bring it to life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Animate is a word with two jobs. As a verb, to animate means to make drawings or models seem to move, or to make something more lively. As an adjective, animate means alive or living.
explain: «The students animated a short cartoon about a frog, one drawing at a time.» Here animate is a verb: the drawings are made to seem to move. Ask yourself what the children did. They made the drawings move, so animate means to make something seem to move.
explain: «Scientists sorted the objects into animate and inanimate things.» A dog is animate because it is alive, and a rock is inanimate because it is not. The opposite of animate is inanimate, so the prefix in- works like "not" here.
fact: Animate can be a verb or an adjective.
fact: The verb forms are animate, animates, animated and animating.
fact: As a verb, «animate» means to make drawings or models seem to move in a film or cartoon.
fact: As an adjective, «animate» means alive or living, and its opposite is «inanimate».
fact: An «animated film» is a film made from drawings or models that seem to move.
exercise: «The class will animate a short cartoon about a frog.» What does animate mean here? | Sleep under a blanket | *Make drawings seem to move in a film | Paint the classroom walls blue | Stop a film from playing
exercise: What is the opposite of animate, meaning not alive? | animal | *inanimate | animated | animator
exercise: «Her funny story animated the whole class.» What does animated mean here? | Gave the class a test | Sent the class home early | Put the whole class to sleep | *Made the class lively and interested
test: Which word means alive or living? | inanimate | silent | still | *animate
test: «The children animated their models so they seemed to walk.» What does animated mean in this sentence? | *Made to seem to move | Hidden | Dropped | Painted
exam: Which sentence uses animate to mean alive? | «The teacher animated the lesson with games.» | «We will animate the model on Monday.» | *«The fish is animate, but the stone is inanimate.» | «The film was animated by the children.»
